            "review_title": "Review at Loan Mai",
            "review_text": "lilybt\n6167 contributions\n4\nIt tastes distinctly thick.\nAug 2024 • Family\nIt seems to be a popular restaurant among Japanese expats. It is located a block back from the JNR tracks in a corner lined with restaurants called \"Tong Dui Tan Street.\" Hanoi restaurants usually close around 22:00, but many in this area seem to be open all night.\nKomzantom (Shrimp Fried Rice), the expat's recommended menu item, is a different name: egg fried rice, MSG and a black pepper soup with shrimp that tastes extremely rich in crustacean shells. It has a strong taste and MSG, so the beer goes on. The others are deep-fried pigeons and mi sao bo (beef instant fried noodles), another distinctly rich flavor on parade. You'll be thirsty, but the junky flavors aren't as bad as you think in the open air in summer.\nRead more\nTranslated from Japanese\nShow original\nWritten July 8, 2025",
